  "description": "A .NET data layer for Entity Framework Core apps where you declare C# models and nothing else: no DbContext class, no DbSet property, no IEntityTypeConfiguration, no registration, and no IDbContextFactory injected to read a row. A `Model<TId>` base carries Id and a domain-events buffer; a source generator builds the EF model from every one it finds, so nothing is reflected and a trimmed publish cannot drop a table. Reads live on the model type (`Product.Where(...)`, `Product.FindAsync(id)`, `Product.AsQueryable()`) via C# 14 static extension members, always untracked, each on its own short-lived context. The generator also writes a form-shaped `ProductModel` for every entity — its mapped properties and validation attributes, no key — for a form to bind; writes are plain EF Core, a domain method saved through an injected context. Value objects map as EF complex types, strongly-typed ids get a generated value converter, and mapping rules live in a static Configure on the model. Opt-in `ITimestamped` / `ISoftDeletable` / `IVersioned` markers drive audit stamps, transparent soft delete and optimistic concurrency through `ISaveChangesInterceptor`s, with after-commit domain-event publication through Rask.Cqrs. A class that does not derive from Model stays ordinary EF Core.",
